  "summary": "Recent preprints supply polynomial-time, approximation, and exact-solver results for parsimony and triple-consistency problems on phylogenetic networks and…",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is computing or testing ancestral structure under parsimony and consistency criteria on phylogenetic networks and ancestral genomes. One preprint gives polynomial-time algorithms for checking ancestor-based consistency of rooted and anchored triples through least common ancestors, with and without forbidden triples. A second addresses the parental parsimony score problem on binary, tree-child phylogenetic networks, reporting a first constant-factor approximation together with a new exact result. A third preprint, on bioRxiv, develops an exact small parsimony solver for ancestral genome reconstruction under the DCJ-indel model, using an ILP with indel costs and theoretical bounds to shrink the search space. What is new across these is algorithmic tractability: explicit polynomial-time or approximation guarantees for network-level problems, and exact optimization for genome-level reconstruction under a rearrangement model.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-06-29"
}
